<article class="env-lemma" id="0A8A">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0A8A">Lemma <span data-tag="0A8A">75.13.10</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be an algebraic space over $S$. Let $L, K$ be objects of $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. If either </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$L$ in $D^+_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ and $K$ is pseudo-coherent, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$L$ in $D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ and $K$ is perfect, 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> then $R\mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits (K, L)$ is in $D_\mathit{QCoh}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from the analogue for schemes (Derived Categories of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/0A6H" data-tag="0A6H">36.10.8</a>) via the criterion of Lemma <a href="/tag/08F2" data-tag="08F2">75.5.2</a>, the criterion of Lemmas <a href="/tag/08HE" data-tag="08HE">75.13.2</a> and <a href="/tag/08HG" data-tag="08HG">75.13.5</a>, and the result of Lemma <a href="/tag/08JP" data-tag="08JP">75.13.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>